Adds the ability to provide an array of partials with a count parameter to `seedMany()` and `generateMany()` methods. Partials are merged with generated entities by index.

### Usage

```ts

// Create 3 entities, customize only the first
const users = await userFaketory.seedMany(3, [
  { name: 'Alice' }
]);
// Result: 3 entities (first has name 'Alice', others use defaults)

// Works with multiple partials too
const users = await userFaketory.generateMany(5, [
  { email: 'admin@example.com', name: 'Admin' },
  { email: 'user@example.com' }
]);
// Result: 5 entities (first two customized, last three use defaults)
```


### Changes

- ✅ New method signatures: `seedMany(count, partials)` and `generateMany(count, partials)`
- ✅ Partials merged by index (partial at index 0 merges with entity at index 0, etc.)
- ✅ Extra partials ignored if count is less than partials.length
- ✅ Missing partials use defaults if count is greater than partials.length

